text @[Teacher]
text Is that so? I'm so glad.
text The elderly teacher is sympathizing with me.
text He seems happier than I am.
text It was the afternoon during the opening ceremony of the new year when I'd decided to take a job offer.
text It was one of the several jobs he presented to me when I first started searching.
text Every job that I'd searched for myself had turned out fruitless.
text And even the most meager hopes I had were crushed.
text It was a sign of my life to come, so I became depressed.
text Even so, I still had to tell him.
text So I showed myself to the employment bureau.
sound 889.aac
text @[Teacher]
text It calms my soul when a student who came to see me finally decides on their course in life.
sound 88A.aac
text @[Teacher]
text Especially in this school, since there are very few students that come see me.
sound 88B.aac
text @[Teacher]
text I feel as happy as if you were my own child.
sound 88C.aac
text @[Teacher]
text ...
text @[Tomoya]
text Teacher.
text This is the first time I actually talk to this teacher of my own volition.
sound 88D.aac
text @[Teacher]
text Hm?
text @[Tomoya]
text You helped me out a great deal.
text And this is the last thing I will ever say to him.
text I give him my deep gratitude, and leave behind the room filled with the smell of lamp oil in the heater.
